  "narrative": {
    "intro": "8(a) set-aside contracts obligated $9.2B in FY2026 to date. The program recorded 10,030 awards with an average award size of $916K, and obligations fell 32.9% year over year. Yearly totals show a peak in FY24 at $15.1B followed by a decline to $13.7B in FY25 and the current FY26 total of $9.2B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $4.4B through 8(a) set-asides so far in FY2026. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services lead industry demand at $1.1B and $954M respectively, while Facilities Support Services accounts for $900M. Top vendors include ASRC FEDERAL FACILITIES LOGISTICS LLC at $132M and AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC at $118M. Contracting activity is concentrated in services and IT-related NAICS codes, with substantial obligations also in construction and engineering services. Buyers and vendors listed reflect the FY2026 to date ordering pattern and show where procurement volume is concentrated within the 8(a) set-aside market this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in 8(a) obligations this fiscal year?",
        "body": "8(a) set-asides obligated $9.2B in FY2026 to date, down 32.9% year over year. Obligations rose from $11.3B in FY21 to $15.1B in FY24, then fell to $13.7B in FY25 and to $9.2B in FY26. The program issued 10,030 awards so far, with an average award size of $916K. The Department of Defense remains the largest buyer with $4.4B in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who and what are receiving 8(a) dollars?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buying agency at $4.4B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $859M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $788M. Computer Systems Design Services leads industries at $1.1B, Other Computer Related Services follows at $954M, and Facilities Support Services accounts for $900M. ASRC FEDERAL FACILITIES LOGISTICS LLC and AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC lead vendors at $132M and $118M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
